  "question": {
    "text": "For a cell reaction involving a two-electron change, the standard e.m.f. of the cell is found to be $0.295 \\mathrm{~V}$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The equilibrium constant of the reaction at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aZ88w",
      "text": "\n$29.5 \\times 10^{-2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ifLEd",
      "text": "\n10\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "amZVg",
      "text": "\n$1 \\times 10^{10}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ASka6",
      "text": "\n$1 \\times 10^{-10}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The equilibrium constant is related to the standard emf of cell by the expression\n$\\log K=E_{\\text {cell }}^0 \\times \\frac{n}{0.059}=0.295 \\times \\frac{2}{0.059}$\n$\\log \\mathrm{K}=\\frac{590}{59}=10$ or $\\mathrm{K}=1 \\times 10^{-10}$",
    "image": null
  },
